WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.140
After several delays, "Shazam!&nbsp;
Fury of the Gods" is almost here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.820
and fans are hyped. Here's what you and your&nbsp;
"Shazamily" need to know before the big premiere.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.680
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods" has been in the&nbsp;
production pipeline for quite some time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.440
The sequel was announced in April 2019 — right&nbsp;
after the first film hit theaters. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.380
we've been waiting for quite a&nbsp;
while since then. What possibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.540
could have delayed the development of "Shazam 2?"

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.780
Well, possibly a pandemic that shuttered an entire&nbsp;
industry ... and a massive company merger ... and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.280
a complete restructuring of the DC Universe.&nbsp;
You know — a few minor things here and there.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.780
Originally, the movie was supposed&nbsp;
to hit theaters on April 1, 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.680
but hey, April Fools! The film was&nbsp;
then pushed back to November 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:52.080
2022 before getting shuffled off to June 2, 2023,&nbsp;
followed by a new date of December 16, 2022.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.880
Not wanting to compete against the blue-skinned&nbsp;
juggernaut that is "Avatar: The Way of Water,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.580
Warner Bros. pushed "Fury of the Gods" back&nbsp;
yet again, kicking it over to December 21.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:09.360
The sequel was eventually moved yet again to its&nbsp;
(hopefully) final release date of March 17, 2023.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.900
Granted, it's enough to give a&nbsp;
DC fan some serious whiplash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.100
but we're pretty sure it will be worth the&nbsp;
wait when the "Shazamily" soars into theaters.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.540
In the first "Shazam!" film, we&nbsp;
watched a young Billy Batson adopt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.840
his new superhero persona and&nbsp;
battle the evil Doctor Sivana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.820
all while coming to terms with his troubled past&nbsp;
and finding solace with his new foster family.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.280
Now, Billy and his siblings are out in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.840
fighting crime with the powers of literal&nbsp;
gods. Naturally, Billy's got a lot to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.800
about his new abilities — and also needs&nbsp;
to deal with something of an existential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.840
crisis — but things get a lot more complicated&nbsp;
with the arrival of three Greek goddesses.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.780
"The daughters of Atlas are coming to hunt us."

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.940
According to the official plot synopsis,&nbsp;
they're on the hunt for "the magic stolen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.020
from them long ago." That magic just so&nbsp;
happens to give the Shazamily their powers.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.640
Based on the official trailers, it looks like the&nbsp;
goddesses will try to get their hands on a scepter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.920
that looks an awful lot like the one belonging to&nbsp;
the wizard who granted Billy his powers. It also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.180
appears that scepter will give them the ability&nbsp;
to steal the Shazamily's superhero abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.380
and it doesn't help matters any that two&nbsp;
of the daughters, Hespera and Kalypso,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.680
are bringing along a whole bunch of&nbsp;
monsters to wage war on the world.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.540
Interestingly, when it comes to comic book&nbsp;
accuracy, the Daughters of Atlas are a bit of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.640
mixed bag. Atlas himself is a DC Comics character,&nbsp;
although we don't know if he'll be appearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:34.500
in the movie, and so is Athena, who's more&nbsp;
closely aligned with Wonder Woman on the page.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.140
However, Hespera and Kalypso — while hailing&nbsp;
from Greek mythology — are new to the DC mythos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.400
having never appeared in comic book&nbsp;
form before. It'll be interesting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.420
see how these goddesses play out in the&nbsp;
story, although we're guessing Athena&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.320
will eventually shift sides while her&nbsp;
sisters will be pretty solidly bad guys.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.380
There's no "Shazam!" without Zachary Levi. The&nbsp;
adult version of the titular hero is perhaps the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.300
funniest superhero in cinema, and that's thanks&nbsp;
to Levi's natural wit and charms. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.140
Levi will be once again donning&nbsp;
the big red suit and accompanying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.340
his teenage alter ego, Asher Angel as&nbsp;
Billy Batson, in the upcoming movie.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.111
"You want these powers? Come get 'em!"

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:17.460
As for the Greek goddesses, they'll&nbsp;
be portrayed by titans of Hollywood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.320
The villainous Hespera will be played by&nbsp;
the legendary Helen Mirren. Her sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.440
Kalypso, will be portrayed&nbsp;
by the one and only Lucy Liu.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.240
The third goddess is Athena, and she'll be&nbsp;
played by Rachel Zegler, who made a huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:35.100
Hollywood splash with her debut performance as&nbsp;
Maria in Steven Spielberg's "West Side Story."

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:40.800
Character actor extraordinaire Djimon Hounsou will&nbsp;
return as the wizard who gave Billy his superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.720
powers, while Marta Milans and Cooper Andrews&nbsp;
will return as Billy's loving foster parents.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:51.960
David F. Sandberg broke onto the scene with one&nbsp;
of the creepiest short films ever made — 2013's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.980
"Lights Out." He then turned that eerie&nbsp;
little film into a feature-length movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.420
released in 2016. After that, he&nbsp;
revisited the horror genre with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:04.260
"Annabelle: Creation" before lending&nbsp;
his talents to the original "Shazam!"

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.520
Now, Sandberg is back in the director's&nbsp;
chair for "Shazam! Fury of the Gods."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.480
Speaking with Total Film, the filmmaker&nbsp;
explained the movie would be taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.740
a wider approach to the story and its&nbsp;
characters than the first film, saying,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.580
"It's still Shazam's movie, but it's&nbsp;
also about the family. They've all been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:24.600
superheroes for a while now, trying&nbsp;
to stop crime and save people. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.080
they're not very good at it. The city&nbsp;
has dubbed them the Philly Fiascos."

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.760
The original "Shazam!" had pretty much&nbsp;
everything — laughter, tears, screams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:37.740
and explosions. All that goodness was largely&nbsp;
thanks to screenwriter Henry Gayden, who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:42.780
also worked on projects like "Earth to Echo" and&nbsp;
"There's Someone Inside Your House." Never fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.040
Gayden is returning for part two, but he&nbsp;
won't be working solo this time around.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.080
Gayden is joined by Chris Morgan, which seems to&nbsp;
indicate that "Fury of the Gods" will have a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.000
more action. How so? Well, Morgan has penned&nbsp;
the scripts for multiple entries in the "Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.360
&amp; Furious" franchise, including "Tokyo Drift,"&nbsp;
"Fast Five," "Furious 7," and "Hobbs &amp; Shaw."

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:09.840
There's a lot changing in the world of DC. With&nbsp;
James Gunn and Peter Safran in charge, the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.820
universe is getting something of a reboot, with&nbsp;
some superhero movies being canceled and new ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:19.680
on the way. So where does the "Shazam!" series&nbsp;
fit into Gunn and Safran's plans for the future?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.040
"A lot has changed in the last few years …"

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.120
While we don't know for sure if we're&nbsp;
getting a "Shazam! 3," Zachary Levi has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.380
commented on the situation. As covered&nbsp;
by the Hollywood Reporter, Levi took to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:37.020
Instagram in December 2022, defending the two&nbsp;
new DC heads and asking fans to be a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.940
more open to their new direction. He also&nbsp;
gave an update on his own status, saying,

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.600
"I have no idea what's ultimately&nbsp;
going to happen to me. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.840
I'm in a pretty good position. I&nbsp;
think we made a pretty great movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:54.420
and I think it's going to do reasonably well.&nbsp;
I hope so! But again, regardless of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.920
if they decide at some point [to recast me],&nbsp;
then them's the breaks. That's how it goes."

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:03.600
That same month, a distressed fan on Twitter&nbsp;
responded to a rumor that Levi would no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.520
be Shazam, saying they would "throw hands"&nbsp;
to protect Levi's place in the DC Universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.540
The tweet caught Levi's attention, and&nbsp;
the "Shazam!" actor gave this response:

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.180
"Oooh, I really wouldn't go believing everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.360
you see on the internet. I'm&nbsp;
Gucci [...]. We all Gucci."

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.660
Hopefully, we'll figure out soon&nbsp;
enough what Gunn and Safran have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.300
in store for our literal man-child superhero.

